Here is a detailed guide on how to enhance both your LinkedIn Cover Image and your LinkedIn Profile / Exported Resume PDF to make your application stand out to AI recruiters and tech leads.1. LinkedIn Cover Image EnhancementsYour current banner image captures your core technical stack, but a few refinements can make it look much cleaner, more readable, and visually impactful:   Key Adjustments NeededFix Misspellings & Garbled Text: The SQL code snippet on the left contains noticeable typo artifacts (e.g., constor id, naeee esetrongs, peresthquage, language herors'). Replace this with clean, valid SQL code (e.g., standard SELECT ... FROM ... WHERE ...).   Profile Picture Safe Zone: LinkedIn places your circular profile photo on the bottom-left of the banner. Ensure key text like "Llama 3.2" or code snippets aren't covered by your avatar when viewed on desktop or mobile.   Improve Contrast & Hierarchy:Make Dilshan Sathsara and AI & LLM Developer prominent in the center.   Group the key highlights: Text-to-SQL SaaS Engine, Agentic AI & Dynamic Workflows, and RAG Pipelines into clear, clean badges or subheadings.Footer Information: Keep your contact details (Email, GitHub, Education) aligned along the bottom edge with clean icons.   2. Content to Add & Refine in Your Profile / PDFTo turn your profile export into a top-tier candidate resume, add the following key missing sections and details:A. Professional Summary / Headline Fine-TuningHeadline:AI & LLM Developer | Fine-Tuned Llama 3.2 & Text-to-SQL SaaS | Agentic AI & RAG Architectures | Applied Science @ Wayamba UniversityB. Highlighted Technical Projects (Add to Profile/PDF)Your experience description mentions impressive work, but breaking it into distinct, bulleted projects creates high visual impact:Text-to-SQL Enterprise SaaS EngineTech: Llama 3.2 (4-bit LoRA Fine-Tuned), FastAPI, PostgreSQL, LangChain/LlamaIndex.Key Features: Live schema introspection, self-healing SQL query guardrails, and candidate self-consistency voting to eliminate hallucinations before execution.Autonomous Agentic Workflows & Research AgentsDynamic task planning, reasoning loops, tool execution, and web-aware retrieval agents.Synthetic Data Pipeline & RAG InfrastructureBuilt scalable vector search pipelines with custom embeddings and synthetic dataset generation for fine-tuning LLMs.C. Complete Tech Stack CategorizationOrganize your skills clearly so ATS scanners and human readers can evaluate you instantly:CategoryTechnologies & ToolsLanguages & FrameworksPython, FastAPI, LangChain, LlamaIndex, PyTorchAI & LLMsFine-Tuning (LoRA/QLoRA), Llama 3.2, Gemini API, RAG, Autonomous AgentsDatabases & Vector StoragePostgreSQL, Vector DBs (Chroma/Pinecone/Qdrant)Tools & Version ControlGit, GitHub, Docker, Replit, IntelliJ IDEAD. Highlight Applied Science Analytical SkillsQuantify how your degree in Applied Science (Physical Sciences) improves your software engineering capabilities:Mathematical Modeling & Logic: Applying mathematical rigor to prompt evaluation, self-healing algorithms, and ranking metrics.Experimental Data Analysis: Systematic iteration during fine-tuning, loss monitoring, and benchmarking against real production datasets.